-- title:
--   Multidegree zero gives χ=χ(𝒪) on a strict transform
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a package $\mathfrak X :$ `DRModelPackage p`, a discrete valuation domain $O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$, a ring homomorphism `toκ : O →+* κ` which is surjective, and a resolved model package `𝔛reg : DRResolvedModelPackage p 𝔛 O κ toκ`, with total space $Y$, structure morphism `𝔛reg.toBase : Y ⟶ Spec O`, morphism `𝔛reg.toDR` to the base change of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\mathbb Z \to O$, and ideal sheaves `𝔛reg.comp v` indexed by `X0MqComponents 𝔛reg.width`$= \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \oplus \Sigma_{x}\,\mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{width}\,x-1)$. Given $m$ sections $\sigma_j : \operatorname{Spec} O \to Y$ of `𝔛reg.toBase`, exponents $\mathrm{pos}_j,\mathrm{neg}_j \in \mathbb N$ and components $v_j$ such that for each $j$ the image of the closed point of $O$ lies in the open set `𝔛reg.smoothOffEdges` and in the support of `𝔛reg.comp (v j)` but in the support of no other `𝔛reg.comp w`; given $a^+,a^- : \text{components} \to \mathbb N$ with, for every component $c$, $$\sum_j \delta_{v_j = c}(\mathrm{pos}_j-\mathrm{neg}_j) + \sum_{F} (a^+_F-a^-_F)\,\mathrm{inter}(F,c) = 0,$$ the intersection form being that of `x0MqResolvedTable 𝔛reg.width` (all multiplicities $1$, $\mathrm{inter}(i,j) = \mathrm{x0MqAdj}(i,j) - \delta_{ij}\sum_{j'} \mathrm{x0MqAdj}(i,j')$); and given a module $M$ on the base change of `DRModel.toBase p` to $O$ which is invertible (locally isomorphic to the unit module) and whose pullback along `𝔛reg.toDR` is isomorphic to the iterated tensor product $\bigotimes_j \big((\sigma_j)^*\text{ker}^{\mathrm{pos}_j}\big)^\vee \otimes (\sigma_j)^*\text{ker}^{\mathrm{neg}_j}$ tensored with $\big(\prod_F (\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{comp}\,F)^{a^+_F}\big)^\vee \otimes \prod_F (\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{comp}\,F)^{a^-_F}$ (here `invModule` is the dual of `module`, the kernel ideal sheaf module). Let $b \in \mathrm{Fin}\,2$, let $e$ be an isomorphism from the base change along `Spec.map toκ` of `(𝔛reg.comp (Sum.inl b)).subschemeι ≫ 𝔛reg.toBase` to the curve `(𝔛.ratModel κ).C`, compatible with the projections in the sense that $e$ followed by `(𝔛.ratModel κ).toBase` is `pullback.snd`, and let $\mathcal V$ be a two-affine-open cover of that curve. Then the Čech Euler characteristic over $\kappa$, computed from $\mathcal V$ and the structure morphism of `𝔛.ratModel κ`, of the pullback of $M$ along `inv e` followed by `pullback.fst`, the closed immersion of the subscheme of `𝔛reg.comp (Sum.inl b)` and `𝔛reg.toDR`, namely $\dim_\kappa H^0 - \dim_\kappa H^1$, equals the same quantity for the unit module on that curve.
--
--   This is the Euler-characteristic computation for a divisorial sheaf of total multidegree zero on the regular model of $X_0(p)$: restricted to either strict transform of the special fibre, such a sheaf has the same Čech Euler characteristic as the structure sheaf, the horizontal contributions of the sections $\sigma_j$ and the contributions of the exceptional and strict-transform components cancelling by the multidegree hypothesis. It feeds the identification of the fibre of a multidegree-zero divisorial sheaf on the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model, [`ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.isAlgEquivZero_fibre_of_pullback_toDR_iso_divisorial_of_multidegree_eq_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.isAlgEquivZero_fibre_of_pullback_toDR_iso_divisorial_of_multidegree_eq_zero).
